</ul><hr data-start="4635" data-end="4638"><h2>Cost of Living in Canada for Nepali Students</h2><div class="TyagGW_tableContainer"><div tabindex="-1" class="group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit"><table data-start="4688" data-end="4798" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="4688" data-end="4727"><tr data-start="4688" data-end="4727"><th data-start="4688" data-end="4703" data-col-size="sm" class="last:pe-10">Expense Type</th><th data-start="4703" data-end="4727" data-col-size="sm" class="last:pe-10">Average Monthly Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="4738" data-end="4798"><tr data-start="4738" data-end="4773"><td data-start="4738" data-end="4754" data-col-size="sm">Accommodation</td><td data-start="4754" data-end="4773" data-col-size="sm">CAD 700 – 1,500</td></tr><tr data-start="4774" data-end="4798"><td data-start="4774" data-end="4781" data-col-size="sm">Food</td><td data-start="4781" data-end="4798" data-col-size="sm">CAD 250 – 500</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p data-start="4841" data-end="4949">| Transportation | CAD 80 – 150 |<br>
| Internet & Utilities | CAD 100 – 200 |<br>
| Miscellaneous | CAD 200 – 400 |</p><p data-start="4951" data-end="5048">Average annual living expenses can range between CAD 12,000 and CAD 20,000 depending on the city.</p><hr data-start="5050" data-end="5053"><h2>Scholarships for Nepali Students in Canada</h2><p data-start="5101" data-end="5130">Popular scholarships include:</p><ul data-start="5131" data-end="5316">
