                'faqs' => '[{"question":"Which UK university is best for Nepali students?","answer":"The University of Manchester, University of Edinburgh, University of Warwick, and University of Leeds are among the most popular choices due to their academic quality, support services, and strong employability outcomes."},{"question":"What is the most affordable UK university for Nepali students?","answer":"Universities such as Leeds, Sheffield, and Birmingham generally offer comparatively affordable tuition fees and living costs."},{"question":"Can Nepali students get scholarships in UK universities?","answer":"Yes. Nepali students can apply for Chevening Scholarships, Commonwealth Scholarships, GREAT Scholarships, and university-specific scholarships."},{"question":"Is IELTS mandatory for UK universities?","answer":"Many universities require proof of English proficiency. However, some institutions may accept alternative qualifications depending on eligibility criteria."},{"question":"Which UK university has the highest graduate employability?","answer":"Universities such as Oxford, Cambridge, Imperial College London, Warwick, and Manchester consistently perform strongly in graduate employability rankings."},{"question":"How much does it cost to study in the UK from Nepal?","answer":"Tuition fees typically range between \\u00a320,000 and \\u00a340,000 per year, depending on the university and program. Living expenses vary by city and lifestyle."},{"question":"Can Nepali students work while studying in the UK?","answer":"Yes. International students are generally allowed to work part-time during academic sessions and full-time during official vacation periods, subject to visa regulations."},{"question":"Which courses are most popular among Nepali students in the UK?","answer":"Business Management, Computing, Data Science, Engineering, Finance, Healthcare, and Artificial Intelligence are among the most sought-after programs."}]',
                'quick_info_items' => '[]',
